---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';

export const lastUpdated = '2026-10-15';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — What Data DevSnap Collects"
  description="How DevSnap handles data. The tools run in your browser, nothing you paste is uploaded, and there are no tracking cookies."
  schemas={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Privacy Policy — What Data DevSnap Collects',
    url: `${SITE.domain}/privacy/`,
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.author },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.publisher },
  }}
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
    <ol class="crumbs">
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li>Privacy Policy</li>
    </ol>

    <header class="tool-hero">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The short version: the tools run in your browser, nothing you paste is ever
        uploaded, and there are no tracking cookies on this site.
      </p>
      <p class="updated-note">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose mt-3">
      <h2>1. What this site does with your input</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing. Every tool on {SITE.name} is implemented in JavaScript that runs inside
        your browser. The value you paste into a tool is processed by the page you are
        looking at and is never transmitted to us, because there is no endpoint that
        would receive it.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can verify this independently: open your browser's developer tools, switch
        to the network panel, and use any tool. The only request that appears is the
        one that loaded the page.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Server logs</h2>
      <p>
        Like any web server, the host that serves this site keeps standard access
        logs containing the requested URL, the referring page, the browser's
        user-agent string, the request timestamp and the IP address. These logs are
        used for security and to keep the site running, are retained for a short
        period, and are not combined with any profile of you.
      </p>
      <p>
        A tool's input never appears in those logs, because it is never sent.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Advertising and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site is funded by advertising. Third-party vendors, including Google, use
        cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the internet.</li>
        <li>You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
        <li>You can opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalised advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not set our own tracking cookies, we do not operate a behavioural
        advertising system, and we do not build a profile of you across sites. We do
        use privacy-friendly, aggregate traffic measurement to understand which
        pages are useful.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We record aggregate, non-identifying usage data such as which pages are
        visited and which country the request came from, in order to know which
        tools are worth maintaining. This data is not used to build a profile of
        individual visitors and is not shared with third parties.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Local storage</h2>
      <p>
        Some tools remember a preference, such as the theme you selected in the
        snapshot tool or the options you chose in a formatter. That state is stored
        in your browser's local storage, on your device, and is never sent to us. You
        can clear it at any time through your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-party content</h2>
      <p>
        Pages may contain outbound links to other websites. Once you follow one, that
        site has its own privacy policy and its own data practices, over which we
        have no control.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a developer utility and is not directed at children. We do not
        knowingly collect personal information from anyone, of any age.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct or
        delete personal data we hold about you, or to object to its processing. Since
        we do not collect personal information beyond standard server logs and
        aggregate analytics, there is very little to request. If you have a question
        anyway, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially, the date at the top of this page changes
        with it. We will not retroactively apply a weaker policy to data collected
        under a stronger one.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
